WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.146
Fala was bent over a tubular device when Zann and his friends walked in.

2
00:00:17.147 --> 00:00:20.937
"You're alive!" she cried, rushing over to hug them.

3
00:00:20.938 --> 00:00:24.343
"When I got back here and you were gone, I feared the worst!"

4
00:00:24.344 --> 00:00:28.663
"Sorry," Perda said sheepishly. "We should've left you a note."

5
00:00:28.664 --> 00:00:31.282
Fala stepped back and glared at them.

6
00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:38.801
"Yes, you should have," she scolded. "Never mind—I'm just glad you're okay. But we have a problem."

7
00:00:38.802 --> 00:00:42.823
"You're right," Zann said. "We were just at the palace."

8
00:00:42.824 --> 00:00:45.735
"What's going on at the palace?" asked Fala.

9
00:00:45.736 --> 00:00:49.059
Zann and the others told Fala what had happened.

10
00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:53.361
Fala nodded when they got to the part about Morb appearing in the throne room.

11
00:00:53.362 --> 00:00:57.490
"One of my contacts at the palace was supposed to check in an hour ago.

12
00:00:57.491 --> 00:01:00.977
When I didn't hear from him, I used the Remote Eye."

13
00:01:00.978 --> 00:01:07.405
She gestured at the device. "I saw Morb walking around in the throne room.

14
00:01:07.406 --> 00:01:11.204
But the Eye doesn't have sound, so I couldn't hear what he was saying."

15
00:01:11.205 --> 00:01:13.985
"Did you see Yog?" Zann asked.

16
00:01:13.986 --> 00:01:17.150
"No," Fala replied. "I hope he's safe.

17
00:01:17.151 --> 00:01:19.954
And I'm glad you kids got out when you did."

18
00:01:19.955 --> 00:01:25.079
"We almost didn't," Gliss told her. "We ran into a troll on our way out."

19
00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.493
"Well, Zann did, anyway," Perda added.

20
00:01:28.494 --> 00:01:32.780
That reminded Zann of the silver talisman. He described it to Fala.

21
00:01:32.781 --> 00:01:38.981
"Do you think Morb could be using talismans to send extra power to the trolls?" he asked.

22
00:01:38.982 --> 00:01:43.911
"That sounds like something I've seen in the ancient texts." Fala looked intrigued.

23
00:01:43.912 --> 00:01:50.807
"Such talismans wouldn't only provide extra power—they could also be a way for Morb to control the trolls.

24
00:01:50.808 --> 00:01:57.396
If only we could get our hands on one of those talismans. It could be invaluable to us."

25
00:01:57.397 --> 00:02:03.866
"Yeah, well, good luck finding someone crazy enough to go up to a troll and take it," said Perda.

26
00:02:03.867 --> 00:02:07.467
"So what should we do now?" Zann asked Fala.

27
00:02:07.468 --> 00:02:10.078
"We freed a lot of Reds earlier.

28
00:02:10.079 --> 00:02:14.388
If we all work together, maybe we can stop Morb."

29
00:02:14.389 --> 00:02:22.193
Fala looked worried. "Most of those Reds aren't ready to face Morb yet. They're staying hidden, not using magic.

30
00:02:22.194 --> 00:02:26.180
Venna and her people are trying to devise a plan." She shrugged.

31
00:02:26.181 --> 00:02:31.040
"Maybe you kids should head home—you'll be safer there until we figure out what to do.

32
00:02:31.041 --> 00:02:33.088
Do you have a way to get there?"

33
00:02:33.089 --> 00:02:37.797
"We rode here on dragons," Darb said. "We left them grazing in the forest."

34
00:02:37.798 --> 00:02:42.532
"We're not going home—I don't have a home to go to," Zann said.

35
00:02:42.533 --> 00:02:46.542
"My grandfather was taken and so were Gliss' parents."

36
00:02:46.543 --> 00:02:52.455
Gliss nodded. "Swamp Bottom isn't any safer than First City. We're staying here."

37
00:02:52.456 --> 00:02:57.092
"All right," said Fala. "But it's getting late—let's get some sleep.

38
00:02:57.093 --> 00:03:00.393
Tomorrow could be a very long day."

39
00:03:00.394 --> 00:03:04.628
Late that night Morb stood alone in the palace courtyard.

40
00:03:04.629 --> 00:03:09.339
Sweat poured off his forehead as he focused every bit of energy he could gather.

41
00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:12.940
"Come to me," he murmured.

42
00:03:12.941 --> 00:03:20.235
His entire body shook with effort. With the magic he'd taken from all those Reds, was he strong enough to do this?

43
00:03:20.236 --> 00:03:24.400
His energy began to waver. Sharp pains were shooting through him.

44
00:03:24.401 --> 00:03:29.980
But he'd waited too long for this moment—he wouldn't wait any longer. It had to be now!

45
00:03:29.981 --> 00:03:34.552
Morb's knees buckled as he focused every ounce of energy on his task.

46
00:03:34.553 --> 00:03:38.300
Falling to the ground, he writhed back and forth in agony.

47
00:03:38.301 --> 00:03:44.241
And that was all it took. The extra bit of friction shot through him.

48
00:03:44.242 --> 00:03:48.655
"Yes!" he gasped as he felt his energy shift.

49
00:03:48.656 --> 00:03:49.680
Crash!

50
00:03:49.681 --> 00:03:52.397
His eyes popped open and he smiled.

51
00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:57.833
His masterpiece, the new machine, stood before him in all its evil glory.

52
00:03:57.834 --> 00:04:06.417
Its enormous frame of wire and bone gleamed in the starlight, and the paralyzer pythons writhed angrily in their glass prison.

53
00:04:06.418 --> 00:04:12.266
Morb climbed to his feet, still shaking from the effort of moving the machine all the way from the fortress.

54
00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:15.179
For a moment he considered summoning Wyssa.

55
00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:21.958
He only needed a few more items, starting with the Skellian sea sponge she'd promised to bring him tomorrow.

56
00:04:21.959 --> 00:04:26.422
If he ordered her to fetch it now, the machine would be complete that much sooner.

57
00:04:26.423 --> 00:04:30.804
But he decided to wait. After all, what was one more day?

58
00:04:30.805 --> 00:04:37.416
Very soon now, he would have everything he'd ever dreamed of back in his pathetic Void days.

59
00:04:37.417 --> 00:04:44.480
When Zann awoke the next morning, his friends were eating puckerberry pancakes. Zing was slurping dragon mush nearby.

60
00:04:44.481 --> 00:04:48.124
"We didn't want to wake you," Perda said when Zann sat up.

61
00:04:48.125 --> 00:04:50.868
"We figured you needed the extra sleep."

62
00:04:50.869 --> 00:04:55.253
Darb grinned. "Plus Perda wanted to eat all your pancakes."

63
00:04:55.254 --> 00:04:59.889
Zann hurried over to them. "Where's Fala?" he asked, grabbing some food.

64
00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:03.231
"She was gone when we woke up," Gliss said.

65
00:05:03.232 --> 00:05:06.979
"She left a note telling us to stay here until she gets back."

66
00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:11.647
Zann didn't say anything. He finished his breakfast and then headed toward the door.

67
00:05:11.648 --> 00:05:14.519
"Where are you going?" Perda asked.

68
00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:18.221
"I want to see what's going on outside," Zann replied.

69
00:05:18.222 --> 00:05:23.087
When he turned the doorknob, it started spinning so fast that he couldn't hold onto it.

70
00:05:23.088 --> 00:05:26.412
Then a little toy bird popped into view.

71
00:05:26.413 --> 00:05:29.762
"Nice try, kids," it said in Fala's voice.

72
00:05:29.763 --> 00:05:36.722
The others laughed, but Zann frowned. He thought about trying to find a way to breach Fala's spell.

73
00:05:36.723 --> 00:05:39.664
But without using magic, it seemed hopeless.

74
00:05:39.665 --> 00:05:44.851
He realized he had no choice but to stay there as she'd asked—at least for a little while.

75
00:05:44.852 --> 00:05:49.895
Luckily he didn't have to wait too long. Fala burst in 15 minutes later.

76
00:05:49.896 --> 00:05:54.013
"What's wrong?" Zann asked when he saw the grim look on her face.

77
00:05:54.014 --> 00:06:03.388
"I've been out gathering the latest news," Fala replied. "It's not good."
